@startuml
title TraceLeft System Architecture

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 220

node "Linux Host (Target)" {
  node "User Space" {
    component "TraceLeft CLI" as CLI
    package "TraceLeft Library" as Lib {
      component "Probe Loader" as ProbeLoader
      component "Userspace Tracer" as Tracer
      component "Handler Map Manager" as MapMgr
      component "Event Dispatcher" as Dispatcher
      component "Generator" as Generator
      component "Config Parser" as ConfigParser
      component "gobpf Integration" as GoBPF
    }
    artifact "Event Registration\n{ProgramID, Pids, ELFPath}" as EventReg
    file "Event Config Metadata\n(Proto/JSON: position, type, name, suffix, hash_func)" as ConfigMeta
    artifact "Generated eBPF Handler Source" as GenSource
    artifact "Common Event Header Definition" as CommonHdr
  }

  node "Kernel Space (Linux Kernel >= 4.11)" {
    component "eBPF Main Program" as BPFMain
    component "Handler eBPF Programs" as Handlers
    collections "Handler Maps\nhandle_NAME_progs\nhandle_NAME_progs_ret" as HandlerMaps
    collections "Return Program Maps\n(keyed by process context)" as ReturnMaps
    interface "kprobe/kretprobe hooks" as Kprobes
    queue "perf event channel" as Perf
  }
}

CLI --> ConfigParser : parse CLI args
ConfigParser --> EventReg
CLI --> ProbeLoader : execute 'trace' command
EventReg --> ProbeLoader : register programs/processes
EventReg --> Tracer : start session for PIDs

ConfigMeta --> Generator : read configuration
Generator --> GenSource : generate handler source

ProbeLoader --> GoBPF : load BPF object, maps\nattach probes
MapMgr --> GoBPF : update handler maps\n(default and process-specific)
Tracer --> GoBPF : subscribe/read perf events

GoBPF --> BPFMain : load & attach to hooks
GoBPF --> Handlers : load handler programs
GoBPF --> HandlerMaps : create/update maps
GoBPF --> ReturnMaps : create/update maps
GoBPF --> Kprobes : attach kprobe/kretprobe

BPFMain --> HandlerMaps : select handler program
BPFMain --> ReturnMaps : select return handler
Handlers --> Perf : emit events
Perf --> Tracer : deliver events
Tracer --> Dispatcher : dispatch by common header

Dispatcher ..> CommonHdr : uses for userspace dispatch
Handlers ..> CommonHdr : prepend to emitted events

ProbeLoader ..> GenSource : consume generated handlers (optional)

note right of Perf
perf-based event channel for kernel->userspace events
end note

note right of HandlerMaps
Handler naming:
- maps: handle_NAME_progs, handle_NAME_progs_ret
end note

note right of Kprobes
Probe naming:
- kprobe/handle_NAME
- kretprobe/handle_NAME
end note

note bottom of BPFMain
No handler set => return 0 (no-op)
end note

note top of GoBPF
Implementation remains based on 'gobpf'
end note

note right of Handlers
Event types: syscall, file, network
Default and process-specific handlers supported
Each event includes the common leading section
end note
@enduml
